-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, four power armors (printed 133-140 and 144-146): Protege, Red Hawk, Sabre, Samson Missileman
-- 4 vehicle rows, with 43 locations and 14 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~311-northern-gun-2-power-armor-g.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-x209-protege', 'Protege (Sammy Jr.) Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum, at 20% of the normal fatigue rate and 10% below 50 mph (80 km). Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high or across unassisted; the jet boosters carry it 100 ft (30.5 m) high and lengthwise; each +50% with a running start. Not flight.', 'None. At the top of a leap it can hold position for one melee round (15 seconds) before drifting back down, and it lands on a cushion of air.', 'Sinks; walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots). Maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m).', 'Man-sized: height 6-7.6 ft (1.8 to 2.3 m), by the buyer''s size; width 4 ft 6 in (1.4 m); length 2-3 ft (0.6 m)', '422 lbs (190 kg)', 230, 1, NULL, 650000, '1.4 million credits nuclear, 1 million Solid Oxide, 650,000 electric; the lowest is stored. Silver plating the forearm Vibro-Sword is 8,000 more (gear row ng-x209-protege-silver-plating).', 'Model Type: NG-X209 Mk I. Class: Armored Infantry Assault Suit. Known on the street and among mercenaries as Sammy Junior. For years NG''s customers asked above all for a man-sized suit modelled on the Samson, and the team of Jeanette Spahr, Rebecca R. Northhaven and Rallon Cheswat built one: it looks and fights much like the bigger Samson, minus its big rail gun and mini-missile launcher, so the two work well side by side. A best seller among power armors since it came out in Summer 109 P.A., and liked by men-at-arms and adventurers of every kind. Its 230 M.D.C. main body is among the heaviest for a suit its size. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: only what belts and backpacks hold. Power: nuclear, 15 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric versions are priced. Handheld weapons: any side arm, Vibro-Knife, Neural Mace, shotgun, grenades, flares or anti-monster gear, kept in belt pouches and holsters (up to two belts), a bag or a backpack, with rifles slung by a strap. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector giving any E-Clip weapon unlimited payload. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352), Robot P.S. 28: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Cat-like landings: back and leg thrusters set it down safely from as high as 300 ft (91.4 m), half that if the main back thrusters are destroyed; from 300 to 600 ft (183 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions, on 11-20 no harm or delay; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 6D6 S.D.C./Hit Points to the wearer and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Features beyond the standard: two abdomen searchlights (4 M.D.C. each) on a 20 degree arc, as spotlight or narrow beam, 200 ft (61 m); two simple helmet cameras storing 96 hours of video and 4,000 stills; a mouthpiece loudspeaker with language translator and 20-voice modulator; and passive nightvision (1,600 ft/488 m) with ultraviolet vision.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.133-136'),
  ('ng-11f-red-hawk', 'Red Hawk Flying Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 60 mph (96 km) maximum, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high or across unassisted; jet-assisted, 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 200 ft (61 m) across without taking flight.', 'Hovers in place up to 400 ft (122 m); flies at 290 mph (464 km) maximum, cruising at 150 mph (240 km). Super-thruster: 490 mph (784 km) for 90 seconds with combat bonuses halved, six times an hour before an automatic cut-out stops it. Ceiling 2,000 ft (610 m), or 4,000 ft (1,219 m) on the super-thruster, settling back to 2,000 afterward. The jets must cool after at most eight hours aloft; unlimited range with rest stops.', 'Cannot fly underwater; swims about 4 mph (6.4 km) or walks or runs the bottom at 15 mph (24 km). Maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m).', 'Height about 8 ft (2.4 m) to the head, 9 ft (2.7 m) including the thruster pack; width 4 ft (1.2 m) wings folded, 13 ft (4 m) spread; length 4 ft 8 in (1.42 m)', '550 lbs (247.5 kg)', 192, 1, NULL, 1000000, '2 million credits for a new nuclear suit, rail gun, ammo and missiles included; 1.5 million Solid Oxide; 1 million electric battery; the lowest is stored. Availability is poor to fair at most NG outlets away from Ishpeming, good at Kingsdale and Arzno, and excellent at Ishpeming/Upper Michigan and MercTown.', 'Model Type: NG-11F Red Hawk PA. Class: Armored Flying Infantry Assault Suit. Released in the winter of 108 P.A. while NG works on new designs to follow the Samson, which cannot truly fly and is ageing. Its jets and wings are an open copy of the original Coalition SAMAS (NG prefers inspired), yet the CS has never objected, and rumor holds that Ishpeming licensed the design or struck a secret deal, maybe even building SAMAS for the CS; the book says the NG-CS relationship is in fact closer than most suppose, that Ishpeming''s own forces use variants of this suit and of the Blue Hawk, and points to the Juicer Killer (p.106). Roughly the old SAMAS''s equal, behind the newer CS models of the Tolkeen siege, it adds a heavy super-thruster for short bursts of speed and altitude. Otherwise it looks nothing like a SAMAS: a reinforced bird-of-prey helmet shielded from behind by the thruster housing, scythe-like blades in the forearms, and an optional short-range laser or mini-missile launcher on either arm or both. Popular with mercenary companies, independent armies and kingdoms'' forces, and with bandits, raiders and pirates. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life (its flying range line says 15 years); Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are priced. Hand to hand per Basic or Flying Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), Robot P.S. 28: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), power dive punch 3D6 (two attacks, with every combat bonus but strike halved, roll with impact included), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Sensors and features: the standard set only.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.136-138'),
  ('ng-uelx42-sabre', 'Sabre Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum, reached from a standstill in 24 seconds, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 12 ft (3.7 m) high or across.', 'None without a back jet pack, sold at extra cost.', 'Swims or walks the bottom at half its land speed, at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 2,000 ft (610 m).', 'Man-sized: height generally 5.6-7 ft (1.7 to 2.1 m); width 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m); length 2 ft (0.6 m)', '215 lbs (97 kg)', 180, 1, NULL, 587000, '898,000 credits nuclear, 587,000 Solid Oxide; the lowest is stored. No electric battery version, the UEL drawing too much power; nuclear outsells Solid Oxide three to one. One Vibro-Saber with waist belt and scabbard is included, and for now NG takes 50% off one more Vibro-Blade, energy rifle or pistol bought with the suit. An extra thigh UEL is 160,000 more (gear row ng-uelx42-thigh-uel).', 'Model Type: NG-UELX42. Class: Medium Armored Infantry Exoskeleton with UEL. Designed by Neil Wager, Chad Thompson and M. Wilson: a sleek, light, affordable man-sized suit, more like a high-tech version of a knight''s plate than a gun platform, with no protruding built-in guns, sensor pods, big backpacks or heavy thrusters to throw it off balance. It was the first suit to carry NG''s Universal Energy Link, in the summer of 108 P.A.: with no weapons of its own it powers nearly any E-Clip weapon or tool made in North America, whoever built it, including guns picked up or taken from a foe, saving the owner clips, recharges and the cost of built-in weapons. Buyers were doubtful at first, then sales of UEL suits rose 900% and are expected to grow fourfold again within six months, which is why newer NG suits carry it. The usual kit is an energy rifle (particle beam or plasma for heavy damage) and a Vibro-Saber on the belt, often with a side arm, a second saber or a Vibro-Knife; back fittings take an NG Environmental Backpack, a jet pack or an ammo canister for a rail gun or grenade launcher. Popular with mercenaries, town garrisons, militias and bandits for its price and protection, and with Wilderness Scouts, spies, field scientists and adventurers who want armor without bulk. Robot P.S. 26. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 10 year average life; Solid Oxide priced. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector that powers a weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. a blast, with a breaker that shuts off anything stronger. Hand to hand per Basic or Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), Robot P.S. 26: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., normal punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: helmet multi-optics with passive nightvision and infrared (1,600 ft/488 m) and thermal optics (1,000 ft/305 m); rubbery palm and finger grips worth +2% to all Climbing skills, those from Acrobatics and Gymnastics included; and rubber-tread soles that grip well and quiet its steps, so Acrobatics, Climbing, Gymnastics, Prowl, Swim and similar skills take none of the usual armor penalty. The weight is printed 215 1bs, read as pounds.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.139-140'),
  ('ng-x13-samson-missileman', 'Samson Missileman Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 80 mph (128 km) maximum, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 5 ft (1.5 m) high or 10 ft (3 m) across despite the missile racks; it has no foot or rear jet boosters.', 'None.', 'Cannot swim; walks or runs the sea floor at up to 20 mph (32 km). Maximum depth 2,000 ft (610 m).', 'Height 11 ft (3.4 m), 16 ft (4.9 m) with the Scissor launchers raised to fire; width 5 ft 6 in (1.7 m); length 5 ft 6 in (1.7 m)', '900 lbs (405 kg), fully loaded', 285, 1, NULL, 1200000, '1.2 million credits new and fully powered, with rail gun, one ammo drum and a full load of missiles. Nuclear only: there is no Solid Oxide version yet and electric does not suit it. Poor availability, being a specialist suit.', 'Model Type: NG-X13 Samson Missileman. Class: Armored Infantry Assault Suit. Artillery infantry power armor released in the spring of 107 P.A. by Lorne Wheeler, C. Bellaire and A. Okamura, so that foot soldiers can face tanks, giant robots, supernatural horrors and other heavily armored targets that portable launchers and ordinary power armor struggle against: a walking pillbox of missiles. It is a Samson Mk II chassis with heavier plating and launchers on the back, shoulders and forearms; the extra weight grounds it (the text says it cannot leap, the statistics allow a short one), so it is best screened by infantry or by lighter, faster power armor or flyers. Popular with mercenary outfits that do heavy fighting and attack fortified positions, and with anti-robot specialists. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 15 year average life. Handheld weapons: it seldom carries other heavy power armor or cyborg guns, though it can; man-sized weapons must be altered (bigger handles, trigger guard removed) and are still -2 to strike in its hands. Extras go in hand, slung on a strap or in a bag, with an oversized Vibro-Sword possible in a waist scabbard, and a footlocker-sized compartment inside holds the pilot''s own human-scale weapons. Hand to hand per Basic or Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), Robot P.S. 28: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., normal punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Sensors: everything standard to power armor and to the Samson Mk III, with a complete optics package added: laser targeting, telescopic sight to x10 (2 miles/3.2 km), passive nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m) and thermal imaging (1,000 ft/305 m). Robot Combat and sensor bonus: +1 to strike.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.144-146');

